<title>SINGAPORE: Vitol wins India's March gasoline tender - source.</title>
<headline>Vitol wins India's March gasoline tender - source.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch trader Vitol was the winner of state-owned Indian Oil Corp's (IOC) March gasoline tender, in which it bought 90,000 tonnes of 87-octane leaded grade for delivery at the equivalent of $40 per tonne over Mideast naphtha spot quotes on a cost and freight (c-and-f) basis, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>A company source was unable to reveal the exact price formula of the award which he said was made on a combination of prices.</p>
</text>
